y","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has a return value, that value is also used as"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the return value for the "},{"code":"withMemoryRebound(to:capacity:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"type buffer: The buffer temporarily bound to instances of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"name":"body"}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The return value, if any, of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure parameter.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this method when you have a buffer slice to raw memory and you need","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to access that memory as instances of a given type ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Accessing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory as a type ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" requires that the memory be bound to that type.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A memory location may only be bound to one type at a time, so accessing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same memory as an unrelated type without first rebinding the memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is undefined.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" within the re-bound region may be initialized or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uninitialized. The memory underlying any individual instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must have the same initialization state (i.e.  initialized or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uninitialized.) Accessing a ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose underlying memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in a mixed initialization state shall be undefined behaviour.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the byte count of the original buffer slice is not a multiple of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the stride of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":", then the re-bound buffer is shorter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the original buffer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After executing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":", this method rebinds memory back to its original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding state. This can be unbound memory, or bound to a different type."}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The buffer slice’s start address must match the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"alignment of "},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (as reported by ","type":"text"},{"code":"MemoryLayout<T>.alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). That is,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int(bitPattern: base.baseAddress+startIndex) % MemoryLayout<T>.alignment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must equal zero.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A raw buffer slice may represent memory that has been bound to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a type. If that is the case, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"ty